      "title": "Tensor decoupling · Stop smushing headlines",
      "minutes": 15,
      "tagline": "Labelled layers on one bulletin board",
      "goals": [
        "Describe tensor decoupling as labelled layers, not one mega-cause.",
        "Compute a shelf weight from the Φ rule and read it as a dashboard dial.",
        "File “co-timed” fixtures correctly: shared board, not shared cause."
      ],
      "body": "<p>Walk past any community bulletin board and you will see the failure mode this lesson fixes. A concert flyer overlaps a lost-cat notice which overlaps a city-council agenda, and a hurried reader could invent a story connecting all three: the cat fled the concert the council approved. Human minds are connection machines — give us co-located headlines and we will manufacture a cause. <strong>Tensor decoupling</strong> is the corpus’s discipline against exactly that: put related headlines on one board, yes, but with <em>labelled layers</em>, so that sharing a board is never mistaken for sharing a cable.</p>\n<h3>The layered board</h3>\n<p>In the tensor paper, the 99-octave ladder is sketched as <strong>eleven brackets × nine slots</strong> — eleven broad bands, each holding nine positions, spanning the full 01–99 range. Each layer of the board carries its own label: which claim tier it belongs to, which domain it files, what would count as evidence for it. Solar headlines, model-training milestones, and voyage story beats may all be pinned to the same dated column — <em>co-timed</em> — while the labels keep their causal independence intact. The board records that things happened in the same season; it refuses to whisper that one made the others happen.</p>\n<h3>Shelf weights are dials, not constants</h3>\n<p>The paper equips each shelf with a weight following the rule <em>w<sub>n</sub> = w₀ / Φ<sup>n</sup></em>: each octave step down divides the weight by the golden ratio. What is this weight <em>for</em>? Conversation routing and dashboard emphasis — deeper shelves get geometrically less default attention, the way a newspaper gives page one more ink than page nineteen. It is a <strong>dashboard dial</strong>, tunable and honest about being tuned. It is not a coupling constant, not a measured decay rate, and not a rival to anything in CODATA. The Φ in the denominator is the nesting key from the map — architectural, not physical.</p>\n<div class=\"worked-example\">\n<p>Compute one dial by hand. Let the base weight be w₀ = 1 and take Φ ≈ 1.618. Then w₁ = 1 / 1.618 ≈ <strong>0.618</strong>. For w₂, divide again: 0.618 / 1.618 ≈ <strong>0.382</strong>. For w₃: 0.382 / 1.618 ≈ <strong>0.236</strong>. Notice two things a physicist’s eye would enjoy. First, w₁ + w₂ = 0.618 + 0.382 = 1.000 — a tidy golden-ratio identity (1/Φ + 1/Φ² = 1) that makes the dials sum nicely, which is precisely why Φ was chosen as the <em>filing</em> key. Second, and more important: nothing in that arithmetic touched a laboratory. We tuned an attention dial. If tomorrow the engineers preferred w<sub>n</sub> = w₀ / 2<sup>n</sup>, the catalog would re-route and no experiment anywhere would notice. That replaceability is the signature of a dashboard dial as opposed to a physical constant.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"misconception\">\n<p><strong>The mix-up:</strong> “Two things filed on the same dated board — a solar event and a model release, say — are being claimed as cause and effect.”</p>\n<p><strong>The correction:</strong> Co-timed means <em>same column of the calendar</em>, nothing more. The tensor paper’s whole purpose is decoupling: labelled layers exist so co-location can never quietly become causation. Magma does not move model weights, and the paper says so on its own honesty rail.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"key-terms\"><dl>\n<dt>Tensor decoupling</dt><dd>The discipline of filing related headlines as labelled independent layers on one board, so shared timing is never mistaken for shared cause.</dd>\n<dt>Shelf weight (w<sub>n</sub> = w₀/Φ<sup>n</sup>)</dt><dd>A tunable attention dial that gives deeper octaves geometrically less default emphasis in routing — a dashboard setting, not a physical constant.</dd>\n<dt>Co-timed</dt><dd>Sharing a calendar column on the board. A statement about when, never about why.</dd>\n</dl></div>",
