      "minutes": 15,
      "tagline": "One squeeze story · three domains · SM left standing",
      "goals": [
        "Retell the copper-pipe squeeze Soft Story without claiming SM overthrow.",
        "Define “Soft Story” as a claim tier and say what promotes or demotes one.",
        "Separate the proposed research lanes from finished datasets."
      ],
      "body": "<p>There is a tabletop demonstration beloved of physics teachers everywhere: drop a strong magnet down a copper pipe. Copper is not magnetic — nothing grabs the magnet — and yet it falls in slow motion, drifting down as if the pipe were filled with honey. The real physics (Lenz’s law: the falling magnet induces currents that oppose its motion) is century-old, measured, and beautiful. The Higgs Gate paper borrows that image for the most openly ambitious <em>story</em> in the corpus — and, precisely because the ambition is large, this lesson leans harder on tier discipline than any before it.</p>\n<h3>One squeeze, three domains</h3>\n<p>The unified edition tells a single “squeeze” story across three domains that ordinarily never share a page: <strong>cosmic deceleration talk</strong> (the universe’s expansion history discussed as if something resists free coasting), <strong>mass</strong> (in the Standard Model, particles acquire mass through interaction with the Higgs field — the celebrated, measured physics of 2012), and <strong>conscious presence</strong> (the felt “Now,” framed as awareness being gently braked into a shared present). The story’s claim: these three rhyme — each is a kind of copper-pipe squeeze, a free fall turned into slow, local, present motion. It is, by the paper’s own labelling, a <strong>Soft Story</strong>: an interpretive narrative that coordinates imagery across domains without asserting shared mechanism.</p>\n<h3>What “Soft Story” buys and what it costs</h3>\n<p>Read the tier label as a precise instrument, not a hedge. A Soft Story <em>buys</em> the right to coordinate vocabulary — to let a conversation about attention borrow the dignity of the eddy brake without footnoting every sentence. It <em>costs</em> the right to claim mechanism: the paper states plainly that the <strong>Standard Model is left standing</strong> — the measured Higgs physics is neither challenged nor extended — and that consciousness is not being identified with electroweak symmetry breaking. Alongside the story, the paper lists proposed research lanes (a pipe-squeeze protocol, hydrogen-line RF work, a somatic array) filed under Amendment-A language: <em>proposed</em>, meaning no finished SI datasets exist. Proposal and result are different tiers, and the paper keeps them on separate shelves itself.</p>\n<aside class=\"honesty-rail\"><strong>Honesty.</strong> The Soft Story does not prove consciousness is electroweak symmetry breaking. Story ≠ lab certification; proposed lanes ≠ finished datasets; the SM Higgs keeps its Nobel physics untouched.</aside>\n<div class=\"worked-example\">\n<p>Practise the skill this paper demands: reading an honesty boundary <em>before</em> the poetry can carry you. Open the Higgs Gate paper below and find its boundary section. Extract three facts, in order. <strong>Fact one — genre:</strong> the document self-labels as Soft Story unification, narrative tier. <strong>Fact two — the standing structure:</strong> an explicit sentence leaves the Standard Model intact; no measured physics is contested. <strong>Fact three — the lanes:</strong> three research directions are listed as proposals, with no datasets attached. Now do the thing most readers skip: write one sentence in your own words that a sceptical friend would accept — for example, “This paper tells one deliberately labelled story connecting mass, cosmology, and attention through a squeeze image, proposes experiments it has not run, and touches no measured physics.” If your sentence survives the friend, you have read the paper at its own declared tier. That is the whole skill.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"misconception\">\n<p><strong>The mix-up:</strong> “A paper connecting the Higgs field to consciousness is claiming physics discovered the soul — or it is pseudoscience pretending to.”</p>\n<p><strong>The correction:</strong> Both readings ignore the label on the tin. The paper claims a <em>story</em> — labelled Soft, coordinating imagery across domains — and explicitly declines mechanism: the SM stands, no dataset is asserted, the lanes are proposals. Judged as what it says it is (narrative-tier unification imagery with honest rails), it neither discovers souls nor pretends to.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"key-terms\"><dl>\n<dt>Soft Story</dt><dd>A named claim tier: an interpretive narrative coordinating vocabulary across domains, with mechanism claims explicitly declined.</dd>\n<dt>Eddy brake (Lenz image)</dt><dd>The copper-pipe demonstration — real, measured physics — borrowed as the squeeze image threading the three domains.</dd>\n<dt>Amendment-A lanes</dt><dd>The proposed research directions (pipe squeeze, hydrogen-line RF, somatic array) — proposals with no finished SI datasets, filed as such.</dd>\n</dl></div>",
